{
    "background_story": "Harvey was a skilled carpenter with a passion for restoring old houses. He had a special fondness for adding dormer windows to the rooftops of his projects, which he believed brought a touch of elegance and whimsy to the structures. One day, Harvey inherited an old Victorian mansion from a distant relative, and he saw it as the perfect opportunity to showcase his craft. He spent months renovating the property, carefully adding dormer windows to the attic space to create a cozy retreat with breathtaking views of the surrounding countryside. As he worked, Harvey discovered a hidden journal belonging to the original owner of the house, who had also been a carpenter. The journal revealed a family secret: the dormer windows had been a symbol of good fortune and prosperity for generations. Harvey felt a deep connection to the history of the house and continued to honor the tradition, making the dormer windows a signature feature of his future projects.",
